{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00569",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.15,
      "end_seconds": 8.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "G'day, you're Chloe Nakamura, yeah? Just checking I've got the right file open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.62,
      "end_seconds": 23.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Yes, that's me. Hi, doctor. Sorry, I'm a bit nervous. I've been googling and it's all gone a bit dark."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.84,
      "end_seconds": 32.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Ha, Dr Google has never helped anyone sleep. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.55,
      "end_seconds": 41.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "I'm gaining weight and I don't know why. I'm eating the same as always, if anything less."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.09,
      "end_seconds": 48.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "How much are we talking about, and over how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.59,
      "end_seconds": 60.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.82,
      "text": "About six kilos, I think? But when did it start... I honestly can't say. Maybe winter, maybe before that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.36,
      "end_seconds": 74.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.13,
      "text": "Not knowing is fine. Lots of people only notice when their jeans stop doing up. Has anything changed at work or home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.48,
      "end_seconds": 83.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "I work night shifts at the hospital, a few months now. Everything's upside down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.68,
      "end_seconds": 95.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "That can muddle your body clock. Your file says you take a thyroid tablet. Remind me what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.39,
      "end_seconds": 105.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "For my underactive thyroid. Levothyroxine, 75 micrograms, once a day, every morning before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.97,
      "end_seconds": 112.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Good. And you take it every single day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.66,
      "end_seconds": 127.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.13,
      "text": "Yes, every morning. Well, most mornings. On night-shift days I honestly can't tell if I've taken it. I worry I've doubled up or missed it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.3,
      "end_seconds": 145.57,
      "duration_seconds": 15.27,
      "text": "That's very common, and we'll sort it. Think of the thyroid as the thermostat in a house. If the heater's patchy, the whole place runs cool and slow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.55,
      "end_seconds": 150.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "So that could explain the weight?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.22,
      "end_seconds": 160.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "It could. Let me ask about the rest of you. How are your bowels?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.81,
      "end_seconds": 166.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Fine. Regular as clockwork, oddly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.21,
      "end_seconds": 174.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Good. Any pounding heart or palpitations, or feeling shaky?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.65,
      "end_seconds": 180.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No palpitations. Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.97,
      "end_seconds": 189.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Okay. Any allergies I should have on file before we go further?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.68,
      "end_seconds": 202.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.74,
      "text": "Yes, actually, that's something I wanted to ask. I'm allergic to penicillin. I came out in hives when I was about twenty."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.33,
      "end_seconds": 215.64,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "That's well worth having on the file. And your thyroid tablet is nothing like penicillin, so there's no clash there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.43,
      "end_seconds": 224.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "What if I need an antibiotic one day? Will they know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.77,
      "end_seconds": 236.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "It's flagged on your record, so any prescriber will see it, and I'd remind them anyway. Penicillin, hives. Remember those two words."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.21,
      "end_seconds": 243.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Okay, that helps. Can an allergy like that fade over time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.44,
      "end_seconds": 261.24,
      "duration_seconds": 14.8,
      "text": "Sometimes, yes. Plenty of people grow out of a penicillin reaction, and there are proper ways to test it if it ever matters. For now, we treat it as real."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.39,
      "end_seconds": 272.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "Right. Can we do the checks now? I'd like to know I'm not falling apart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.51,
      "end_seconds": 280.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Righto. Pressure, pulse and weight first, then I'll feel your neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.92,
      "end_seconds": 301.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Pressure is 124 over 78, pulse 62, and weight 82 kilograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.64,
      "end_seconds": 306.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Eighty-two? Is that terrible?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.89,
      "end_seconds": 318.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "It's a number, not a verdict. It matches what you're telling me. Now chin up, I'll feel your thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.09,
      "end_seconds": 338.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Thyroid feels normal in size and smooth. Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.71,
      "end_seconds": 346.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Is that good? Could it be cancer? Sorry, I had to ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.43,
      "end_seconds": 362.95,
      "duration_seconds": 14.52,
      "text": "Nothing I felt points that way. In plain English, I think this is most likely your underactive thyroid not being fully covered, probably because of the patchy doses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.29,
      "end_seconds": 371.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "So I wasn't imagining it. Can't you just put the dose up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.59,
      "end_seconds": 392.02,
      "duration_seconds": 17.43,
      "text": "Not yet. A bigger dose on top of missed ones just makes a rollercoaster. First, lock in the routine. Phone alarm, tablet next to the toothbrush, same time even after a night shift."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.38,
      "end_seconds": 399.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Okay. An alarm. I can do an alarm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.95,
      "end_seconds": 408.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "And give it half an hour on its own before your coffee or breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.48,
      "end_seconds": 414.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much less scared now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.21,
      "end_seconds": 424.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Good on you. Look after yourself, and try to catch some sleep."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.19,
      "end_seconds": 428.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    }
  ]
}
